\subsection{\code{PlanOrder$modify_part()}}{
  Changes one part of the placed plan that has not sent anything yet, such as a bracket's stop before the entry fills.

The part keeps the new values and sends them when its turn comes, and nothing is sent to a broker now. Only a part with a fixed price, a plain limit or a native stop, takes a price, and only a stop takes a trigger price. A part that has already sent its order is changed through \code{TradeableInstrument$modify_order()} with that order's id instead.
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{PlanOrder$modify_part(
  part,
  price = NULL,
  trigger_price = NULL,
  quantity = NULL,
  dry_run = FALSE
)}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Arguments}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="arguments">}}
    \describe{
      \item{\code{part}}{The character path of the part, such as \code{root.each_fill.children.0}, as \code{parts} lists it.}
      \item{\code{price}}{The numeric new limit price in rupees, or \code{NULL} to leave it.}
      \item{\code{trigger_price}}{The numeric new trigger price in rupees of a stop, or \code{NULL} to leave it.}
      \item{\code{quantity}}{The integer new total quantity, or \code{NULL} to leave it. An order that closes a position can only be reduced.}
      \item{\code{dry_run}}{A logical that is \code{TRUE} to have UBI check the change without making it.}
    }
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Details}{
    Errors: signals \code{ValueError} when the order has not been placed, so there is no parent to act on; \code{BadRequestError} when no value was given, the part works its price out from the market, the part is not a stop and was given a trigger price, or a value is off the tick or lot; \code{NotFoundError} when the engine holds no parent with this id, or the plan has no part at this path; \code{ConflictError} when the part has already sent its order (the detail then lists its \code{orders}), is sized by an earlier part's fills, is kept whole, closes a position and was asked to grow, or the plan has finished; \code{ServiceUnavailableError} when the order engine is not running; and another \code{UnifiedBrokerInterfaceError} subclass for any other failure reported by, or on the way to, UBI.
  }
  \subsection{Returns}{
    The named list \code{TradeableInstrument$modify_order()} returns for a part, with \code{parent_id}, \code{synthetic_type}, \code{part}, its \code{state}, the new \code{price}, \code{trigger_price} and \code{quantity}, \code{outcome}, \code{status_message} and \code{intent_id}.
  }
